Z||000006||Nashco||06-23-2001||01:31 AM||||Disc changer???  For the same price as a disc changer you can now get an MP3 player.  Aiwa makes a great little mp3-cd player for about 220 on ebay constantly.  You can get it from Crutchfield for more, about 250 I think.  You can fit more songs on a disc with mp3 compression than on 6 cds.  Also, no extra space required.  With a small cd booklet (10 max, or visor unit that holds 10 would be best) you have about three days worth of noise on tap.  Minimal wiring, cheap, easy, how could you go wrong?<P>Oh, if you don't like the Aiwa unit, there's a (I believe Kenwood) unit for about 500 bucks that has all top of the line specs.  I have the aiwa unit that is basically exactly the same except only cds play, and I really like it, especially for the cost.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||5
Z||000007||AusFiero||06-23-2001||03:31 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by varnster:<BR><B>some where out of the way, I have amps in the<BR>spare tire tub, and a 8" microsub behind pass<BR>seat, where "O" where should my changer go!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>What are the dimensions of it?<P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/fiero5.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A><BR>Need a Subwoofer Console or Speaker Door Pods?||||reg||1
