Z||000015||87GTBro||06-24-2001||12:13 AM||||I installed the Kenwood KDC-MP8017 in my GT!  It is Kenwoods MP3 player...  I am extremely happy with it.  It cost me a grand total of $371.  I installed it myself.<P>The only problem that I am now noticing is that the cheap CDR's get messed up easier in the heat of the day than regular CDs. After a while, the MP3 files will start skipping.<P>Better keep your MP3 files handy on an extra hard drive!<P>As far as sound quality goes, YOU CANT GET ANY BETTER!!!  I have the Fierosound sub install behind passenger seat with 240W amp, 10" sub and power crossover.  Can you say "Sound studio on wheels"?<P>Really nice.  I wish all of you could hear it...||||reg||1
Z||000016||Predator||06-24-2001||09:47 AM||||I have a JVC 12 disc CD changer mounted on the firewall behind the Drivers seat. The wiring runs under the console to the stereo. It is easy to get to to change out CD's, and no one notice's it there when the seat is back. The controller is mounted in front of the cigarette lighter. It works for me. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero4_1.jpg"> ||||reg||6
